package rules

import com.one2drive.projeto1.decision.DecisionContext

// Meta-knowledge: knowledge about the rules themselves, not about driving, that controls
// the inference. Every rule belongs to one phase (agenda-group) of the decision cycle:
//   perception  01-state-updates.drl: sensor events become the current state of the world;
//   decision    the driving rules (fuzzy weather and the move-off state included), which
//               propose decisions;
//   fallback    the two baseline proposals of defaults.drl, once every other rule has had
//               its say.
// This meta-rule runs first in every cycle (the DecisionContext is updated when a cycle
// begins) and stacks the phases so they run in that order: the agenda fires the group on top
// of the focus stack until it is empty, then the next one. Within a phase, salience still
// orders the rules as before.
rule "Control: perceive, then decide, then fall back"
salience 10000
when
    DecisionContext()
then
    drools.setFocus("fallback");
    drools.setFocus("decision");
    drools.setFocus("perception");
end
